"onboarding.card0.title" = "The Valley went quiet";
"onboarding.card0.body" = "You are the last postman. Letters are the only thread left between the people of the clay Valley. The road ahead runs from the Post Office through the Stilts, the Belfry and the Tubs to the Saddle.";
"onboarding.card1.title" = "Steps are the road";
"onboarding.card1.body" = "Put the phone in your pocket and walk. Every real step moves the postman along the road. Chapter one is about 20 thousand steps; the whole game is about 150 thousand.";
"onboarding.card2.title" = "While you walk";
"onboarding.card2.body" = "The postman reaches the stops on his own and takes every letter. Nothing falls out of the bag because there are many. Each tag says where that piece of mail goes. You get quiet notices about meetings and about a letter that has been handed over.";
"onboarding.card3.title" = "Come back and read";
"onboarding.card3.body" = "The journal holds cards about places and people, showing what happened while you were away. Sometimes, at a fork, you choose which way the story will go.";
"onboarding.card4.title" = "So he walks with you";
"onboarding.card4.body" = "The game needs your step count from Health, and notifications when he stops. Steps are only read, never written. The weather follows yours: the system may ask for location; without it, the weather is seasonal.";
"onboarding.card4.body.fake" = "HealthKit is unavailable in the simulator — steps are added with the “+500” button. On a device the game asks to read steps and to send notifications; location for the weather is optional, and you can refuse.";
