"history.title" = "History";
"history.empty" = "Nothing here yet. The postman has not told anything.";
"history.where" = "%@ · step %@";
"history.main.road.title" = "Morning";
"history.main.road.out" = "The postman left the Post Office in the dark. The bag is buckled. The road is ahead.";
"history.main.road.nina" = "Nina writes to Kuzma about the water and the piles they are building up again, and she is sending her son Timofey socks with a double heel. She asks whether he is eating something hot and whether he writes to Lida.";
"history.main.road.mitya" = "Mitya asks Father Pimen for the belfry, for an antenna. On every band, he writes, the hiss is the same, and it ought to be different.";
"history.main.road.vera" = "In the pocket is Vera's requisition no. 23: twelve batteries for an item called K-2. The reason she wrote down is “keeping the mode.”";
"history.main.stilts.title" = "The Stilts";
"history.main.stilts.body" = "At the Stilts Kuzma took Nina's letter. In the margin there is a schoolboy note: that is Mitya's hand, and Mitya is his grandson. The bream, he writes, are gone, off to the Throat. The piles are being built up again.";
"history.main.belfry.title" = "The Belfry";
"history.main.belfry.body" = "Pimen read the request about the antenna and said he would think. The radio is silent the way Mitya writes it: one hiss on every band.";
"history.main.belfry.fortyone" = "Pimen sent an account along for Vera. On the outside, under the string, without opening it: forty-one memorial candles, the customer's wax. Whose order, and why forty-one, the wrapper does not say.";
"history.main.belfry.opened" = "Inside, on the tape, Pimen tells Vera he will bring the candles himself on Thursday. The Us boy is asking for the belfry for an antenna, and so far Pimen has not given it.";
"history.main.ask.title" = "The gate";
"history.main.ask.bag" = "Nina meets him at the gate and asks whether he has delivered it to Timosha. The letter to her son, and the socks, are still in the bag.";
"history.main.ask.post" = "Nina meets him at the gate and asks whether he has delivered it to Timosha. The socks are still at the Post Office.";
"history.main.ask.body" = "Nina meets him at the gate and asks whether he has delivered it to Timosha.";
"history.main.strange.title" = "Box no. 2";
"history.main.strange.body" = "By the well, in box no. 2, there is a reply “from her son.” The letter says the socks have already arrived, and he calls her mummy. The collection mark on the envelope is the Tubs, box 2. That day the postman had not yet reached the Saddle, and Nina's letter to her son was still in his bag. The reply to that letter had already come. Who dropped the reply in, and how it knows about the socks, is not written there.";
"history.main.nii.title" = "The batteries";
"history.main.nii.body" = "Vera has been given the twelve batteries on requisition no. 23. She calls the item K-2, and the reason is “keeping the mode.” So the thing has a mode, and it uses up cells. What the mode is, Vera does not write.";
"history.main.wind.title" = "The bends";
"history.main.wind.chase" = "On the bends the wind pulled Nina's letter to her son out of the bag. The postman caught it by the barrier. The envelope is muddy, and whole. The socks were still with the letter that day.";
"history.main.wind.let" = "On the bends the wind took Nina's letter to her son, socks and all. Where it went is not visible from the road.";
"history.main.saddle.title" = "The Saddle";
"history.main.saddle.sent" = "Nina's letter to her son has been dropped in the box at the Saddle. She is still asking whether he writes to Lida.";
"history.main.saddle.ksenia" = "In the same collection there is a letter “from Ksenia.” The Nizhny Stvor stamp is dated later than today. She asks him not to go down, and she writes “watch your feet” — the same ending as A.L.'s note in this box. The words match. Why they match is not said.";
"history.main.two.title" = "Two voices";
"history.main.two.body" = "In the collection at the Saddle there is a letter to Nina from Timofey. A.L.'s note says it was held up in sorting. He writes about his pay, about Lida, and he asks her to sit down first and eat. The one from box no. 2 called her mummy and wrote that the socks were already there. These are not one voice. Which of the two wrote, the post does not explain.";
"history.main.fuse.title" = "The fuse";
"history.main.fuse.body" = "Vera sent Mitya a 0.25 A fuse and wrote that she took it off the item K-2. Mitya answers: it burned out at once. The wrong one, he writes, or the right one. After that every band is a single hiss again.";
"history.main.roosters.title" = "Until the rooster";
"history.main.roosters.body" = "Kuzma gave Mitya the dead battery from the receiver. On the wrapper: it played until the rooster, and the light was already out. So not everything went silent in the same hour. Why the radio lasted until morning, he does not write. Only “well.”";
"history.main.thursday.title" = "Thursday";
"history.main.thursday.body" = "Pimen will not give Mitya the belfry, and he adds: on Thursdays even less. He encloses an alphabet and a candle-end. What he has on Thursdays, the telegram does not say.";
"history.main.hum.title" = "The hum";
"history.main.hum.body" = "Mitya can hear the receiver again. At 7.3 it does not hiss, it hums, steady, louder at night, quieter on Thursdays. On the other bands it is still the same. He asks what it is. The letter does not give the hum a name.";
"history.main.station.title" = "Another Tima";
"history.main.station.body" = "Another letter arrives “from Tima.” He calls Nina mummy and writes that he works at a radio station. The one that was held up in sorting wrote about his pay and “sit down first.” The mismatch is still there. Whose voice is whose is still not said.";
"history.main.station.box" = "Another letter arrives “from Tima.” He calls Nina mummy and writes that he works at a radio station. It turns the same way as the reply from box no. 2. How he knows the house is not written there.";
"history.main.station.only" = "A letter arrives “from Tima.” He calls Nina mummy and writes that he works at a radio station. There is no second letter beside it yet to set it against.";
"history.main.mark.title" = "The mark";
"history.main.mark.body" = "Kuzma sent Vera an envelope with almost no words. On the sheet is the number 44, and “well.” What he is measuring, the letter does not name.";
"history.main.lamp.title" = "The lamp";
"history.main.lamp.body" = "Pimen sent a telegram: “Two forty. The lamp. I wrote it down.” What lamp, and what he did with it, the line does not say.";
"history.main.lamp.compared" = "Pimen sent a telegram: “Two forty. The lamp. I wrote it down.” That is not “until the rooster,” and it is not morning. Two times sit side by side, and no letter says why there are two.";
"history.main.bell.title" = "The bell";
"history.main.bell.body" = "From the lee side the Belfry bell can be heard. The ringing is even and long, like a count. How many, and of whom, is not signed.";
"history.main.gorge.title" = "The ravine";
"history.main.gorge.body" = "The path leaves the ravine and goes down. Beyond it is raw clay and fog. What is there cannot be seen from the edge.";
"history.main.clean.title" = "A clean envelope";
"history.main.clean.body" = "Below the Throat the road has been washed out. In the clay lay an envelope with no stamp, and thin hooks inside. It belongs in the chance box on the Boardwalk, not back the way he came.";
"history.main.goat.title" = "What the goat was called";
"history.main.goat.body" = "Nina asks Timofey to write plainly what the goat was called. She tells him not to open the jar.";
"history.main.ramka.title" = "Ramka";
"history.main.ramka.body" = "The letter “from Tima” calls the goat Ramka and puts in a label, “Sprats in tomato”. The same question, a different answer.";
"history.main.bearing.title" = "Louder toward the top";
"history.main.bearing.body" = "On the Peat Cut post a note says: louder toward the top. The frame, if he is carrying it, hears the Valley louder than the Reach. Measuring does not make the road longer.";
"history.main.mothers.title" = "In one piece";
"history.main.mothers.body" = "The letter “from Galya” says she received it in one piece. The hooks Galya packed for Mitya are not inside.";
"history.main.fiftyeight.title" = "Fifty-eight";
"history.main.fiftyeight.body" = "Kuzma writes to Vera: the pole already reads fifty-eight, and the water is not falling.";
"history.main.names.title" = "Four names";
"history.main.names.body" = "Mitya made out a piece of the evening bell. Four names, and Us Galya among them. He does not know what they are.";
"history.main.ether.title" = "A scrap of a song";
"history.main.ether.body" = "A radio lies in the reeds. For a moment a song comes out of it, then only noise. Night is not required.";
"history.main.third.title" = "The third nick";
"history.main.third.body" = "Vera accepted the mark 58. It is the third nick. She puts the decision off until the fourth. She calls the hum at 7.3 the transformer.";
"history.main.wall.title" = "A grey wall";
"history.main.wall.body" = "A grey wall stands across the river in the Gullet. Up close it holds a box door, a rim, a thermos and a pass on a string. Nobody says what the wall is.";
"history.main.zorka.title" = "Zorka";
"history.main.zorka.body" = "Nina writes to Vera: the goat was called Zorka. She asks for the truth and does not accuse.";
"history.main.signature.title" = "Ferapont";
"history.main.signature.body" = "In the bundle with no annotation is a refusal sheet. The line reads: Somov Ferapont Ilyich, the Tubs. Nobody circled the signature.";
"history.main.marsh.title" = "The Settling Pool";
"history.main.marsh.body" = "The kettle on the last stake is still warm. Who was here is not said. Farther on, in a break in the fog, are the pipes of the town.";
